        "## 25.7 Interactive: threshold fairness explorer\n",
        "\n",
        "The following interactive illustrates how a single threshold changes accuracy, selection rate, TPR, FPR, PPV, and fairness gaps across two groups.  The scores are synthetic.  The point is to understand the geometry of thresholding, not to claim a universal fairness rule.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.interactive-card}\n",
        "<h3>Thresholding, error rates, and group gaps</h3>\n",
        "<p>Move the threshold and compare group-wise rates.  The model score is a one-dimensional summary $S\\in[0,1]$; the deployed decision is $\\widehat{Y}=1\\{S\\ge t\\}$.</p>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:1rem;align-items:end;\">\n",
        "  <label>Decision threshold t:\n",
        "    <input id=\"ch25-threshold\" type=\"range\" min=\"0.05\" max=\"0.95\" step=\"0.01\" value=\"0.50\" style=\"width:100%;\">\n",
        "    <span id=\"ch25-threshold-label\">0.50</span>\n",
        "  </label>\n",
        "  <label>Group B score shift:\n",
        "    <input id=\"ch25-shift\" type=\"range\" min=\"-0.20\" max=\"0.20\" step=\"0.01\" value=\"-0.05\" style=\"width:100%;\">\n",
