        "These two tables usually point to different thresholds.  This is a mathematical signal that the design decision is not purely technical.\n",
        "\n",
        "## 25.9 Calibration and uncertainty\n",
        "\n",
        "A model score $S\\in[0,1]$ is calibrated if\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "P(Y=1\\mid S=s)=s.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "In practice we approximate this condition using bins.  If bin $B_m$ contains examples whose scores lie in an interval, define\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\operatorname{acc}(B_m)=\\frac{1}{|B_m|}\\sum_{i\\in B_m} y_i,\n",
        "\\qquad\n",
        "\\operatorname{conf}(B_m)=\\frac{1}{|B_m|}\\sum_{i\\in B_m} s_i.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The expected calibration error is commonly estimated by\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\operatorname{ECE}=\\sum_{m=1}^M \\frac{|B_m|}{n}\\left|\\operatorname{acc}(B_m)-\\operatorname{conf}(B_m)\\right|.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Calibration matters because a score of $0.9$ should not merely rank higher than a score of $0.6$; it should mean something probabilistic.  In NLP, calibration is important for moderation, retrieval confidence, question-answering uncertainty, and decision support."
      ],
      "id": "a7556684"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "def calibration_table(y, s, bins=8):\n",
        "    y = np.asarray(y)\n",
        "    s = np.asarray(s)\n",
        "    edges = np.linspace(0, 1, bins + 1)\n",
        "    rows = []\n",
        "    ece = 0.0\n",
        "    for j in range(bins):\n",
        "        left, right = edges[j], edges[j + 1]\n",
        "        if j == bins - 1:\n",
        "            mask = (s >= left) & (s <= right)\n",
        "        else:\n",
        "            mask = (s >= left) & (s < right)\n",
        "        if mask.sum() == 0:\n",
        "            continue\n",
        "        acc = y[mask].mean()\n",
        "        conf = s[mask].mean()\n",
        "        weight = mask.mean()\n",
        "        ece += weight * abs(acc - conf)\n",
        "        rows.append({\n",
        "            \"bin\": f\"[{left:.2f}, {right:.2f}]\",\n",
        "            \"count\": int(mask.sum()),\n",
        "            \"accuracy\": acc,\n",
        "            \"mean_score\": conf,\n",
        "            \"abs_gap\": abs(acc - conf)\n",
        "        })\n",
        "    return pd.DataFrame(rows), ece\n",
        "\n",
        "cal_table, ece = calibration_table(scores[\"y\"], scores[\"score\"], bins=8)\n",
        "cal_table, ece"
      ],
