        "A classifier can have high accuracy and poor calibration.  Conversely, a calibrated classifier may not have the best thresholded accuracy.  These are different mathematical properties.\n",
        "\n",
        "## 25.10 Distribution shift\n",
        "\n",
        "Let $P$ be the training distribution and $Q$ be the deployment distribution.  Distribution shift means\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "P(X,A,Y)\\ne Q(X,A,Y).\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Important special cases include:\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Covariate shift:** $P(X)\\ne Q(X)$ but $P(Y\\mid X)=Q(Y\\mid X)$.\n",
        "- **Label shift:** $P(Y)\\ne Q(Y)$ but $P(X\\mid Y)=Q(X\\mid Y)$.\n",
        "- **Concept shift:** $P(Y\\mid X)\\ne Q(Y\\mid X)$.\n",
        "\n",
        "In text applications, distribution shift appears when a model trained on one source is used on another source: social media versus formal essays, one university's policy pages versus another's, one time period versus another, or one language variety versus another.\n",
        "\n",
        "Under covariate shift, if the density ratio $w(x)=q(x)/p(x)$ is known or estimated, then\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "R_Q(d)=E_Q[L(d(X),Y)]\n",
        "=E_P\\left[\\frac{q(X)}{p(X)}L(d(X),Y)\\right].\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Thus weighted empirical risk can estimate deployment risk:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\widehat{R}_Q(d)=\\frac{1}{n}\\sum_{i=1}^n w(x_i)L(d(x_i),y_i).\n",
        "$$"
      ],
      "id": "c719d8fd"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# A toy covariate-shift example with two text sources.\n",
        "shift_df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    \"source\": [\"train\"] * 6 + [\"deploy\"] * 6,\n",
        "    \"text_type\": [\"short\", \"short\", \"short\", \"long\", \"long\", \"long\", \"short\", \"short\", \"long\", \"long\", \"long\", \"long\"],\n",
        "    \"loss\": [0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1, 1, 0, 1, 1]\n",
        "})\n",
        "\n",
        "train = shift_df[shift_df[\"source\"] == \"train\"]\n",
        "deploy = shift_df[shift_df[\"source\"] == \"deploy\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "p_train = train[\"text_type\"].value_counts(normalize=True)\n",
        "p_deploy = deploy[\"text_type\"].value_counts(normalize=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "weights = train[\"text_type\"].map(lambda z: p_deploy[z] / p_train[z])\n",
        "unweighted_risk = train[\"loss\"].mean()\n",
        "weighted_risk = np.average(train[\"loss\"], weights=weights)\n",
        "deploy_risk = deploy[\"loss\"].mean()\n",
        "\n",
        "pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    \"estimate\": [\"unweighted train risk\", \"weighted train risk\", \"observed deploy risk\"],\n",
        "    \"risk\": [unweighted_risk, weighted_risk, deploy_risk]\n",
        "})"
