        "## 25.12 Selective prediction and abstention\n",
        "\n",
        "Responsible deployment often requires a model not to answer every query.  A selective classifier returns either a prediction or an abstention symbol $\\bot$:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "g(x)\\in\\{0,1,\\bot\\}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "For a confidence score $c(x)$ and threshold $\\tau$, a simple rule is\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "g_\\tau(x)=\n",
        "\\begin{cases}\n",
        "\\widehat{y}(x), & c(x)\\ge \\tau,\\\\\n",
        "\\bot, & c(x)<\\tau.\n",
        "\\end{cases}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Two quantities are central:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\operatorname{coverage}(\\tau)=P(c(X)\\ge \\tau),\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\operatorname{selective\\ risk}(\\tau)\n",
        "=E[L(\\widehat{Y},Y)\\mid c(X)\\ge \\tau].\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Increasing $\\tau$ often decreases risk among answered cases but also decreases coverage."
      ],
      "id": "a1126c72"
    },
