        "Privacy has a utility tradeoff.  As $p$ approaches $1/2$, the released answer becomes more private but less informative.  As $p$ approaches $1$, the answer is accurate but less private.\n",
        "\n",
        "## 25.14 Hallucination, factuality, and RAG responsibility\n",
        "\n",
        "For a generated answer $Z$ to a prompt $X$, factuality cannot be determined from fluency alone.  A response may be syntactically excellent and factually false.  A clean way to describe a retrieval-augmented system is\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "D_1,\\ldots,D_k \\sim r_\\eta(d\\mid x),\n",
        "\\qquad\n",
        "Z\\sim p_\\theta(z\\mid x,D_1,\\ldots,D_k).\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Errors can enter through retrieval or generation:\n",
        "\n",
        "- relevant documents may not be retrieved;\n",
        "- retrieved documents may be outdated, ambiguous, or contradictory;\n",
        "- the generator may ignore retrieved evidence;\n",
        "- the generator may blend evidence with unsupported prior knowledge;\n",
        "- the final answer may omit uncertainty or citations.\n",
        "\n",
        "For mathematical responsibility, it is useful to separate:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "P(\\text{correct answer})\n",
        "=P(\\text{retrieval sufficient})P(\\text{generation faithful}\\mid \\text{retrieval sufficient})+\n",
        "\\cdots.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "This is not a complete causal model, but it forces students to separate retrieval failure from generation failure.\n",
        "\n",
        "## 25.15 AI-assisted auditing workflow\n",
        "\n",
        "AI tools can help audit NLP systems, but they should not replace statistical reasoning.  A useful AI-assisted workflow is:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Ask the AI system to state the task, target variable, decision rule, and possible harms.\n",
        "2. Ask it to propose subgroup variables that might matter.\n",
        "3. Ask it to list plausible distribution shifts.\n",
        "4. Convert the suggestions into mathematical quantities.\n",
        "5. Compute metrics and uncertainty using data.\n",
        "6. Ask the AI system to critique the audit for missing assumptions.\n",
        "7. Document the final human judgment.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-note}\n",
        "AI assistance is useful for brainstorming failure modes and drafting audit checklists.  It is not evidence.  Evidence comes from data, source documents, mathematical definitions, and careful evaluation.\n",
        ":::\n",
