        "The mathematical lesson is that aggregation is a projection.  It can remove information.  Responsible evaluation often requires conditional metrics.\n",
        "\n",
        "## 25.17 Common mistakes\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Treating accuracy as responsibility.** Accuracy is one statistic, not an ethical guarantee.\n",
        "2. **Ignoring the deployment distribution.** A test set estimates performance only for the distribution it represents.\n",
        "3. **Using group metrics without uncertainty.** Small subgroups can produce unstable estimates.\n",
        "4. **Assuming one fairness metric is always correct.** Different metrics encode different choices.\n",
        "5. **Assuming debiasing projection solves bias.** Geometric correction can help but is incomplete.\n",
        "6. **Confusing fluency with factuality.** Language quality does not imply truth.\n",
        "7. **Using AI critiques as evidence.** AI-generated audits must be checked against data and definitions.\n",
        "\n",
